  "summary": "The Elephanta Caves are a rock-cut complex on Elephanta (Gharapuri) Island, near Mumbai, devoted to the cult of Shiva. UNESCO dates their construction to about the mid-5th to 6th centuries AD. Cave 1 is dominated by a 7-metre Sadashiva sculpture showing three aspects of Shiva, called the Trimurti.",
